Add a 400-character limit on the description field in both post-form and post-edit.
Use form invalidation approach — the Publish and Save Draft buttons are disabled
when the limit is exceeded, and a character counter is shown below the textarea.

## post-form.ts and post-edit.ts

In each component, add a computed signal for character count and validity:

  readonly DESCRIPTION_MAX = 400;

  descriptionLength = computed(() =>
    (this.description() ?? '').length
  );

  descriptionOverLimit = computed(() =>
    this.descriptionLength() > this.DESCRIPTION_MAX
  );

  descriptionRemaining = computed(() =>
    this.DESCRIPTION_MAX - this.descriptionLength()
  );

Where this.description() reads from the component's existing description
signal or form field — read the file to confirm the exact signal or
property name before using it.

## post-form.html and post-edit.html

Below the description textarea, add the counter row:

<div class="description-meta">
  <span class="char-counter"
    [class.over-limit]="descriptionOverLimit()">
    {{ descriptionLength() }} / {{ DESCRIPTION_MAX }}
    @if (descriptionOverLimit()) {
      — {{ descriptionLength() - DESCRIPTION_MAX }} over limit
    }
  </span>
</div>

On the Publish button and Save Draft button, add:
  [disabled]="descriptionOverLimit()"

If the buttons already have other disabled conditions (e.g. !title),
combine with OR:
  [disabled]="!title() || descriptionOverLimit()"

Read the existing disabled bindings on both buttons before modifying
to avoid removing existing validation.

